WEBVTT

00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:04,660
Okay, here we are with Stephanie.

00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:09,660
You can introduce yourself and I just said your name is Stephanie, but I'm gonna let us know a little bit about you.

00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:16,660
Okay, my name is Stephanie Riesen. I am a wife and mother of three and I live in De Wain, Iowa.

00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:18,660
Very good.

00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:29,660
So can you tell us what brought you to Connor's clinic, how you kind of came up all to finding Dr. Connor's and why you maybe chose alternative as your care of choice?

00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:45,660
Yes. Okay, so I became sick in 2015 in March and I was in the hospital for a week. Afterwards, I was referred to three different specialists, a cardiologist, neurologist and gastroenterologist.

00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:57,660
After about six weeks of visiting with those specialists, I kind of went full circle and was referred to the place that I began.

00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:14,660
I really wasn't getting any answers and just felt like I needed somebody that could look at me as a whole person and not just my specific issues individually.

00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:27,660
Yes. That was when a friend called and suggested that I might possibly have Lyme. I began doing some research and thought that she was right.

00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:43,660
So that my search led me to Dr. Connor's here in Minnesota and he was really the first person that was able to see me as a whole person and I really appreciated his holistic approach.

00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:57,660
He diagnosed me with Lyme and put me on some supplements and started me on a new diet and I began to get better for the first time in a long time.

00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:12,660
I was really grateful for his approach. He was kind, caring, easily accessible, just made me feel very comfortable here in his office.

00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:17,660
Yeah, excellent. Would you recommend Connor's clinic to others?

00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:32,660
Yes, I would and I have. A good friend of mine was also sick with Lyme about the same time I was. She took a more traditional approach and was pretty much bedridden and in a wheelchair.

00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:43,660
When she came to see Dr. Connor's, she's been working with him for a few years now and has progressed from a wheelchair to a walker to now not needing anything.

00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:53,660
And she's improving as well. And so I'm thankful that she was able to find the help that she needed as well.

00:02:53,660 --> 00:03:11,660
Excellent. Do you have any primary points of encouragement for somebody who may be just stumbling upon our website for the first time or maybe just kind of at the beginning stages of looking for some alternative care, anything to encourage them on their journey?

00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:24,660
Yeah, I would just say to be prayerful about their decision and just trust God's leading. For me, it was a more alternative path.

00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:41,660
And I think my struggle with that at times has been doubt and sometimes gilting people, their people gilting me into maybe a more traditional path when I've tried the traditional path just hasn't felt good to me.

00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:58,660
But what I do love about Conor's Clinic is that they meet you where you're at. And so, you know, if you want to take a more integrative approach and maybe you're already seeing an oncologist and you want to continue with that, they meet you where you're at and walk through it with you.

00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:16,660
I appreciate that. I'm getting ready for an upcoming surgery that isn't really, you know, an alternative thing. It's more traditional. It's a hysterectomy. And they're helping me through that as well. And so, I'm grateful that they meet you where you're at.

00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:19,660
Perfect.

00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:24,660
Yes. Very good. Thank you, Stephanie.

